1
00:00:01,311 --> 00:00:03,309
<i>Coco (thinking): Don't let Kip find out!</i>

2
00:00:03,163 --> 00:00:04,855
<i>Grandpa Shelby (thinking): He must never know...</i>

3
00:00:04,709 --> 00:00:06,774
<i>Max (thinking): Tonight... everything changes.</i>

4
00:00:06,824 --> 00:00:07,718
Kip: Wait...

5
00:00:07,718 --> 00:00:09,820
I can hear what everyone is THINKING?!

6
00:00:15,471 --> 00:00:16,186
Narrator: One morning,

7
00:00:16,186 --> 00:00:17,709
a few hours earlier...

8
00:00:17,759 --> 00:00:18,604
Max: Kip!

9
00:00:18,604 --> 00:00:19,836
Watch this!

10
00:00:19,836 --> 00:00:21,618
My best throw ever!

11
00:00:21,668 --> 00:00:22,766
Kip: Last time you did that,

12
00:00:22,766 --> 00:00:24,141
you broke my window.

13
00:00:24,191 --> 00:00:25,874
Max: That was one time!

14
00:00:25,924 --> 00:00:27,212
Kip: It was four times.

15
00:00:27,212 --> 00:00:28,217
This week.

16
00:00:34,188 --> 00:00:35,356
Max: ...Did I just knock a star

17
00:00:35,356 --> 00:00:36,646
out of the sky?

18
00:00:36,696 --> 00:00:37,733
Kip: You knocked a STAR out of

19
00:00:37,733 --> 00:00:38,570
the sky!

20
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:39,863
Kip: Whoa... it's warm.

21
00:00:39,863 --> 00:00:40,964
And it's humming.

22
00:00:41,014 --> 00:00:42,337
Max: Don't touch it!

23
00:00:42,337 --> 00:00:44,340
What if it's radioactive?

24
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:46,328
What if it's an alien egg?!

25
00:00:49,139 --> 00:00:50,667
Kip: Ow... my ears are buzzing.

26
00:00:50,667 --> 00:00:52,341
Max, did you say something?

27
00:00:52,391 --> 00:00:53,288
Max: Nope.

28
00:00:53,288 --> 00:00:55,011
I'm totally fine.

29
00:00:55,011 --> 00:00:56,694
Not hungry at all.

30
00:00:56,744 --> 00:00:58,273
<i>Max (thinking): I'm SO hungry.</i>

31
00:00:58,273 --> 00:01:00,225
<i>I could eat a whole pizza.</i>

32
00:01:00,225 --> 00:01:01,526
<i>With the box.</i>

33
00:01:01,576 --> 00:01:02,685
Kip: ...You're hungry.

34
00:01:02,735 --> 00:01:04,321
Max: How did you know that?

35
00:01:04,371 --> 00:01:05,566
Kip: You just said it.

36
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:06,714
"With the box."

37
00:01:06,764 --> 00:01:08,912
Max: I did NOT say that out loud!

38
00:01:08,962 --> 00:01:10,567
Kip: Okay... think of a number.

39
00:01:10,567 --> 00:01:11,542
Any number.

40
00:01:11,592 --> 00:01:12,551
<i>Max (thinking): Seven.</i>

41
00:01:12,551 --> 00:01:14,118
<i>No, too easy.</i>

42
00:01:14,118 --> 00:01:15,732
<i>Eleventy-twelve!</i>

43
00:01:15,782 --> 00:01:17,627
Kip: Eleventy-twelve isn't a number.

44
00:01:17,677 --> 00:01:18,590
Max: AAAH!

45
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:20,392
You're inside my head!

46
00:01:20,392 --> 00:01:21,436
Get out!

47
00:01:21,436 --> 00:01:23,154
It's messy in there!

48
00:01:23,204 --> 00:01:24,178
Kip: Max...

49
00:01:24,178 --> 00:01:25,399
I think this star lets me

50
00:01:25,399 --> 00:01:26,460
read minds.

51
00:01:26,510 --> 00:01:27,966
Max: That's the coolest thing that has

52
00:01:27,966 --> 00:01:29,091
ever happened.

53
00:01:29,091 --> 00:01:30,956
And also the scariest.

54
00:01:31,006 --> 00:01:31,915
Kip: Come on!

55
00:01:31,915 --> 00:01:33,879
Let's test it on somebody else!

56
00:01:34,179 --> 00:01:35,091
Grandpa Shelby: Ah.

57
00:01:35,091 --> 00:01:37,075
Good morning, boys.

58
00:01:37,075 --> 00:01:38,030
Lovely day...

59
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:39,626
for a slow walk.

60
00:01:39,676 --> 00:01:41,262
<i>Grandpa Shelby (thinking): Now where on earth did I</i>

61
00:01:41,262 --> 00:01:42,810
<i>put my glasses?</i>

62
00:01:42,810 --> 00:01:44,969
<i>I've been looking since breakfast.</i>

63
00:01:45,019 --> 00:01:45,610
Kip: Good morning,

64
00:01:45,610 --> 00:01:46,645
Grandpa Shelby.

65
00:01:46,645 --> 00:01:47,712
Your glasses are on top of

66
00:01:47,712 --> 00:01:48,620
your head.

67
00:01:50,130 --> 00:01:51,358
Grandpa Shelby: Hm?

68
00:01:51,358 --> 00:01:52,963
Well, I'll be.

69
00:01:52,963 --> 00:01:54,247
How did you know I was

70
00:01:54,247 --> 00:01:55,772
looking for them?

71
00:01:55,822 --> 00:01:57,717
Max: He reads minds now!

72
00:01:57,717 --> 00:01:58,895
I knocked a star out of

73
00:01:58,895 --> 00:01:59,847
the sky!

74
00:01:59,897 --> 00:02:01,100
Grandpa Shelby: A star?

75
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:02,351
Oh, my.

76
00:02:02,351 --> 00:02:03,983
A Thinking Star.

77
00:02:03,983 --> 00:02:05,594
I read about these when I

78
00:02:05,594 --> 00:02:07,199
was only ninety.

79
00:02:07,249 --> 00:02:09,521
Max: Can you read minds too, Grandpa?

80
00:02:09,571 --> 00:02:10,411
Grandpa Shelby: At my age,

81
00:02:10,411 --> 00:02:11,237
young man,

82
00:02:11,237 --> 00:02:13,488
I can barely read a menu.

83
00:02:13,538 --> 00:02:14,620
Kip: So it's real?

84
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:16,102
I can really hear thoughts?

85
00:02:16,152 --> 00:02:17,733
Grandpa Shelby: Every thought, Kip.

86
00:02:17,733 --> 00:02:18,638
But remember:

87
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:20,714
a thought is like a cloud.

88
00:02:20,714 --> 00:02:21,650
It drifts by,

89
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:23,183
and you only ever see one

90
00:02:23,183 --> 00:02:25,144
small piece of the sky.

91
00:02:25,194 --> 00:02:26,363
<i>Grandpa Shelby (thinking): Oh no.</i>

92
00:02:26,363 --> 00:02:27,840
<i>If he can hear thoughts...</i>

93
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:29,840
<i>he'll find out about tonight!</i>

94
00:02:29,890 --> 00:02:31,504
Kip: Find out about what tonight?

95
00:02:31,554 --> 00:02:32,782
Grandpa Shelby: Hm?

96
00:02:32,782 --> 00:02:33,877
Nothing!

97
00:02:33,877 --> 00:02:35,377
Nothing at all.

98
00:02:35,377 --> 00:02:36,022
Oh look,

99
00:02:36,022 --> 00:02:37,332
a butterfly!

100
00:02:37,382 --> 00:02:39,013
<i>Grandpa Shelby (thinking): Think about turnips.</i>

101
00:02:39,013 --> 00:02:40,643
<i>Think about turnips.</i>

102
00:02:40,643 --> 00:02:42,803
<i>Turnips, turnips, turnips...</i>

103
00:02:42,853 --> 00:02:44,431
Kip: He's thinking about turnips.

104
00:02:44,431 --> 00:02:45,848
Really, really hard.

105
00:02:45,898 --> 00:02:47,404
Max: That's suspicious.

106
00:02:47,404 --> 00:02:50,025
Nobody thinks about turnips that hard.

107
00:02:50,325 --> 00:02:51,779
Coco: Kip, darling!

108
00:02:51,779 --> 00:02:53,368
Max, sweetie!

109
00:02:53,368 --> 00:02:54,588
Fabulous morning,

110
00:02:54,588 --> 00:02:55,689
isn't it?

111
00:02:55,689 --> 00:02:57,013
Gorgeous!

112
00:02:57,013 --> 00:02:58,863
Simply gorgeous!

113
00:02:58,913 --> 00:03:00,897
<i>Coco (thinking): Act normal, Coco.</i>

114
00:03:00,897 --> 00:03:02,374
<i>Act normal.</i>

115
00:03:02,374 --> 00:03:04,720
<i>Don't mention the big secret.</i>

116
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:06,739
<i>And don't look at the hedge.</i>

117
00:03:06,789 --> 00:03:08,673
Kip: Coco... what's behind the hedge?

118
00:03:08,723 --> 00:03:09,928
Coco: Hedge?

119
00:03:09,928 --> 00:03:11,336
What hedge?

120
00:03:11,336 --> 00:03:12,813
I have never seen a hedge

121
00:03:12,813 --> 00:03:14,430
in my entire life!

122
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:16,081
Max: You're literally standing in front of

123
00:03:16,081 --> 00:03:16,968
a hedge.

124
00:03:17,018 --> 00:03:19,169
Coco: That is a SHRUB, sweetie.

125
00:03:19,169 --> 00:03:21,356
A very exclusive shrub.

126
00:03:21,406 --> 00:03:22,958
<i>Coco (thinking): Poor little Kip.</i>

127
00:03:22,958 --> 00:03:23,766
<i>After tonight,</i>

128
00:03:23,766 --> 00:03:25,217
<i>nothing will ever be the same</i>

129
00:03:25,217 --> 00:03:26,165
<i>for him.</i>

130
00:03:26,215 --> 00:03:27,882
Kip: ...Nothing will ever be the same?

131
00:03:27,932 --> 00:03:29,342
Coco: Gotta run!

132
00:03:29,342 --> 00:03:30,833
Busy, busy!

133
00:03:30,833 --> 00:03:32,225
Toodle-oo!

134
00:03:34,036 --> 00:03:35,127
Max: Okay.

135
00:03:35,127 --> 00:03:36,572
That was weird.

136
00:03:36,572 --> 00:03:38,370
Even for Coco.

137
00:03:38,671 --> 00:03:40,003
<i>Mailman (thinking): Did anybody see me trip over</i>

138
00:03:40,003 --> 00:03:40,883
<i>that curb?</i>

139
00:03:40,737 --> 00:03:42,587
<i>Lady (thinking): I hope it doesn't rain.</i>

140
00:03:42,587 --> 00:03:44,687
<i>My hair frizzes when it rains.</i>

141
00:03:44,541 --> 00:03:45,239
<i>Baker (thinking): Is that...</i>

142
00:03:45,239 --> 00:03:46,042
<i>my shadow...</i>

143
00:03:46,042 --> 00:03:47,211
<i>or a raccoon?</i>

144
00:03:47,065 --> 00:03:47,692
<i>Jogger (thinking): Left, right,</i>

145
00:03:47,692 --> 00:03:48,406
<i>left, right...</i>

146
00:03:48,406 --> 00:03:50,008
<i>wait, which one is my left?</i>

147
00:03:49,861 --> 00:03:51,050
<i>Dog Walker (thinking): Too bright!</i>

148
00:03:51,050 --> 00:03:52,239
<i>Too bright!</i>

149
00:03:52,239 --> 00:03:54,133
<i>Who turned on the sun?</i>

150
00:03:54,183 --> 00:03:55,462
Kip: Too many voices!

151
00:03:55,462 --> 00:03:57,554
Everybody's thinking at the same time!

152
00:03:57,604 --> 00:03:59,706
Max: Just think about something quiet.

153
00:03:59,706 --> 00:04:01,039
Like clouds.

154
00:04:01,039 --> 00:04:02,226
Or naps.

155
00:04:02,226 --> 00:04:04,081
Naps are very quiet.

156
00:04:04,381 --> 00:04:05,704
Mom: There you are, sweetie!

157
00:04:05,704 --> 00:04:07,361
Did you have a nice morning?

158
00:04:07,411 --> 00:04:09,313
Kip: Mom... is something happening tonight?

159
00:04:09,363 --> 00:04:10,267
Mom: Tonight?

160
00:04:10,267 --> 00:04:12,173
Oh, just a quiet evening.

161
00:04:12,173 --> 00:04:13,636
Why do you ask, honey?

162
00:04:13,686 --> 00:04:15,504
<i>Mom (thinking): He's growing up so fast.</i>

163
00:04:15,504 --> 00:04:16,664
<i>It's time for him to move</i>

164
00:04:16,664 --> 00:04:18,249
<i>out of his little room.</i>

165
00:04:18,249 --> 00:04:20,363
<i>Tonight, he leaves it... forever.</i>

166
00:04:22,174 --> 00:04:23,399
Kip: ...Okay, Mom.

167
00:04:23,449 --> 00:04:24,819
Mom: Now, why don't you boys go

168
00:04:24,819 --> 00:04:26,844
play far away until sunset?

169
00:04:26,844 --> 00:04:28,186
Very far away.

170
00:04:28,186 --> 00:04:29,718
Really, really far.

171
00:04:29,768 --> 00:04:30,399
<i>Mom (thinking): And please,</i>

172
00:04:30,399 --> 00:04:32,433
<i>please, do not come back early...</i>

173
00:04:32,734 --> 00:04:33,709
Kip: Max...

174
00:04:33,709 --> 00:04:35,660
I think everyone wants me to leave.

175
00:04:35,710 --> 00:04:36,639
Max: What?

176
00:04:36,639 --> 00:04:37,814
No way!

177
00:04:37,814 --> 00:04:39,381
Who told you that?

178
00:04:39,431 --> 00:04:40,695
Kip: Nobody TOLD me.

179
00:04:40,695 --> 00:04:41,765
They THOUGHT it.

180
00:04:41,765 --> 00:04:43,485
Mom wants me out of my room.

181
00:04:43,485 --> 00:04:45,543
Coco says nothing will be the same.

182
00:04:45,543 --> 00:04:47,722
And Grandpa Shelby is hiding something.

183
00:04:47,772 --> 00:04:49,731
Max: Kip, I'm sure there's a good—

184
00:04:49,781 --> 00:04:51,776
<i>Max (thinking): Don't think about the surprise!</i>

185
00:04:51,776 --> 00:04:53,770
<i>Don't think about the surprise!</i>

186
00:04:53,770 --> 00:04:54,998
<i>Bananas!</i>

187
00:04:54,998 --> 00:04:57,226
<i>Bananas, bananas, bananas!</i>

188
00:04:57,276 --> 00:04:59,188
Kip: ...Why are you thinking about bananas?

189
00:04:59,238 --> 00:05:00,414
Max: I'm not!

190
00:05:00,414 --> 00:05:01,482
I'm thinking about...

191
00:05:01,482 --> 00:05:02,706
regular things.

192
00:05:02,706 --> 00:05:04,379
Normal kid things.

193
00:05:04,429 --> 00:05:04,903
<i>Max (thinking): Oh no,</i>

194
00:05:04,903 --> 00:05:05,378
<i>oh no,</i>

195
00:05:05,378 --> 00:05:06,254
<i>oh no.</i>

196
00:05:06,254 --> 00:05:07,359
<i>I wish he would just go</i>

197
00:05:07,359 --> 00:05:08,685
<i>away for a while!</i>

198
00:05:10,696 --> 00:05:11,870
Kip: You too, Max?

199
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:12,625
Max: Wait, Kip,

200
00:05:12,625 --> 00:05:13,963
that's not what I—

201
00:05:15,674 --> 00:05:16,519
Max: Kip!

202
00:05:16,519 --> 00:05:17,570
Come back!

203
00:05:17,570 --> 00:05:18,685
Oh no...

204
00:05:18,685 --> 00:05:20,658
I have to tell the others!

205
00:05:20,958 --> 00:05:22,227
Max: Code red!

206
00:05:22,227 --> 00:05:23,495
Code red!

207
00:05:23,495 --> 00:05:25,999
Kip heard everything and he ran away!

208
00:05:26,049 --> 00:05:27,376
Coco: Everything?!

209
00:05:27,376 --> 00:05:29,682
Even the part about the cake?

210
00:05:29,732 --> 00:05:30,628
Max: No!

211
00:05:30,628 --> 00:05:31,609
Worse!

212
00:05:31,609 --> 00:05:32,790
He thinks we all want him

213
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:33,740
to leave!

214
00:05:33,790 --> 00:05:34,672
Mom: Oh no.

215
00:05:34,672 --> 00:05:36,003
My poor baby...

216
00:05:36,053 --> 00:05:37,527
Grandpa Shelby: Leave it to me.

217
00:05:37,527 --> 00:05:39,190
I know exactly where he goes

218
00:05:39,190 --> 00:05:40,635
when he is sad.

219
00:05:40,635 --> 00:05:42,077
I have known since he was

220
00:05:42,077 --> 00:05:43,219
this tall.

221
00:05:43,269 --> 00:05:44,444
Mom: Hurry, Mr.

222
00:05:44,444 --> 00:05:45,340
Shelby!

223
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:47,859
Grandpa Shelby: Hurrying... is not my specialty.

224
00:05:47,859 --> 00:05:49,632
But I shall try.

225
00:05:52,093 --> 00:05:53,369
Kip: A thought is just one piece

226
00:05:53,369 --> 00:05:54,395
of the sky...

227
00:05:54,395 --> 00:05:56,116
But what if that piece is true?

228
00:05:59,927 --> 00:06:01,838
<i>Coco (thinking): Don't let him find out!</i>

229
00:06:01,692 --> 00:06:03,375
<i>Max (thinking): Go away for a while!</i>

230
00:06:03,228 --> 00:06:04,601
<i>Mom (thinking): He leaves it forever!</i>

231
00:06:04,454 --> 00:06:05,512
<i>Grandpa Shelby (thinking): Turnips!</i>

232
00:06:05,512 --> 00:06:06,595
<i>Turnips!</i>

233
00:06:06,645 --> 00:06:07,504
Kip: Stop!

234
00:06:07,504 --> 00:06:08,441
Stop it!

235
00:06:08,441 --> 00:06:10,064
I don't want to hear anymore!

236
00:06:11,875 --> 00:06:13,299
Grandpa Shelby: There you are.

237
00:06:13,299 --> 00:06:15,727
I came as fast as I could.

238
00:06:15,777 --> 00:06:16,925
Grandpa Shelby: Which, admittedly,

239
00:06:16,925 --> 00:06:18,872
took about three hours.

240
00:06:18,922 --> 00:06:19,786
Kip: Grandpa Shelby...

241
00:06:19,786 --> 00:06:21,331
everyone wants me gone.

242
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:23,258
Grandpa Shelby: A Thinking Star only shows you

243
00:06:23,258 --> 00:06:24,876
the thoughts, Kip.

244
00:06:24,876 --> 00:06:27,353
Never the reasons behind them.

245
00:06:27,403 --> 00:06:28,468
Grandpa Shelby: In all my years,

246
00:06:28,468 --> 00:06:29,577
I've learned this:

247
00:06:29,577 --> 00:06:31,257
when we only hear a little,

248
00:06:31,257 --> 00:06:32,945
we imagine the rest.

249
00:06:32,945 --> 00:06:35,746
And we usually imagine the worst.

250
00:06:35,796 --> 00:06:36,672
Kip: So...

251
00:06:36,672 --> 00:06:37,778
I only heard one piece of

252
00:06:37,778 --> 00:06:38,648
the sky?

253
00:06:38,698 --> 00:06:40,771
Grandpa Shelby: So stop listening with the star...

254
00:06:40,771 --> 00:06:43,209
and come look with your own eyes.

255
00:06:43,209 --> 00:06:44,601
Follow me.

256
00:06:44,901 --> 00:06:45,724
Kip: Hello?

257
00:06:45,724 --> 00:06:46,544
Mom?

258
00:06:46,544 --> 00:06:47,913
Why is it so dark?

259
00:06:48,924 --> 00:06:50,033
Everyone: SURPRISE!

260
00:06:50,083 --> 00:06:51,104
Coco: Happy birthday,

261
00:06:51,104 --> 00:06:52,370
Kip darling!

262
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:54,728
Did you really think we forgot?

263
00:06:54,778 --> 00:06:56,030
Kip: My... birthday?

264
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:57,339
Mom: And that's not all.

265
00:06:57,339 --> 00:06:58,734
Look up, sweetheart.

266
00:07:02,345 --> 00:07:04,180
Mom: Your very own big-kid room.

267
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:04,902
A treehouse,

268
00:07:04,902 --> 00:07:06,600
right outside my window.

269
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,021
You're leaving your little room...

270
00:07:08,021 --> 00:07:09,614
but you're never leaving me.

271
00:07:09,664 --> 00:07:11,009
Kip: So THAT's what you meant...

272
00:07:11,059 --> 00:07:12,578
Coco: "Nothing will ever be the same,"

273
00:07:12,578 --> 00:07:14,534
darling, because now you are officially

274
00:07:14,534 --> 00:07:15,618
a big kid!

275
00:07:15,668 --> 00:07:17,187
Grandpa Shelby: And I am a terrible secret

276
00:07:17,187 --> 00:07:18,598
keeper, so I tried not to

277
00:07:18,598 --> 00:07:20,793
think about the party at all.

278
00:07:20,793 --> 00:07:22,493
Hence... the turnips.

279
00:07:22,543 --> 00:07:23,564
Max: And I needed you to go

280
00:07:23,564 --> 00:07:24,544
away for a while so I

281
00:07:24,544 --> 00:07:25,950
could practice THIS!

282
00:07:30,561 --> 00:07:31,611
Max: Ta-da!

283
00:07:31,611 --> 00:07:33,647
A homemade fireworks show!

284
00:07:33,647 --> 00:07:35,143
And I didn't set anything on

285
00:07:35,143 --> 00:07:36,524
fire... this time.

286
00:07:36,574 --> 00:07:37,549
Kip: Max...

287
00:07:37,549 --> 00:07:38,994
I'm sorry I ran away.

288
00:07:38,994 --> 00:07:39,959
I heard your thoughts,

289
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:41,759
but I didn't listen to your heart.

290
00:07:41,809 --> 00:07:43,178
Max: That's okay.

291
00:07:43,178 --> 00:07:44,891
You're my best friend.

292
00:07:44,891 --> 00:07:47,145
Even when you're inside my head.

293
00:07:47,446 --> 00:07:48,925
Kip: I don't need this anymore.

294
00:07:48,925 --> 00:07:50,385
Thoughts are better when friends share

295
00:07:50,385 --> 00:07:51,575
them on their own.

296
00:07:51,625 --> 00:07:52,821
Max: Then make a wish and let

297
00:07:52,821 --> 00:07:53,667
it go!

298
00:07:58,838 --> 00:08:00,049
Coco: Ooooh.

299
00:08:00,049 --> 00:08:01,409
Oh, my.

300
00:08:01,409 --> 00:08:03,108
Oh, darlings...

301
00:08:03,108 --> 00:08:05,093
I can hear EVERYTHING.

302
00:08:05,143 --> 00:08:05,985
Everyone: Uh-oh.

303
00:08:06,035 --> 00:08:07,893
Coco: Grandpa Shelby!

304
00:08:07,893 --> 00:08:09,679
You think my singing sounds like

305
00:08:09,679 --> 00:08:11,080
a squeaky door?!

306
00:08:11,130 --> 00:08:12,279
Grandpa Shelby: ...Turnips.

307
00:08:15,089 --> 00:08:15,972
Kip: And you?

308
00:08:15,972 --> 00:08:16,868
I don't need a star to

309
00:08:16,868 --> 00:08:18,784
know what you're thinking right now...

310
00:08:18,834 --> 00:08:20,929
Kip: "I want to see the next episode!"

311
00:08:21,230 --> 00:08:21,904
Narrator: Next time:

312
00:08:21,904 --> 00:08:23,372
What if you could shrink to

313
00:08:23,372 --> 00:08:25,079
the size of an ant?
